prompt:
Create one original true-transparent RGBA spritesheet of fifteen full-body right-facing Moxie Capwell dunk-clutch poses, strict 5x3 row-major. Use Moxie's supplied portrait/gameplay refs as canon: adult human woman, pale skin, lavender eyes, thick very long lavender high ponytail with small gold tie, mature athletic anatomy, purple-and-silver uniform with white side panels, purple wristbands and purple high-top shoes. Preserve identity and scale throughout.

1990s arcade basketball pixel-cel art with crisp outlines. Exact 1536x1024 canvas. Fifteen distinct complete figures centered in cells with wide margins and transparent gutters; no overlap, no clipping or edge contact. True-transparent RGBA background. Moxie alone. No ball drawn because gameplay renders it separately. No hoop, rim, net, opponent, court, floor, shadow, glow, effects, background, text or labels.

A clutch dunk: Moxie gathers the invisible ball securely with both hands tight to her chest and keeps it clutched compactly throughout the jump and peak; then opens one hand and releases in a short direct reach at the rim.
0 sprint approach;
1 gather and cup hands tightly at sternum;
2 takeoff tick4 while clutch remains centered at chest;
3 rise with elbows tucked in;
4 knees tuck, both hands guard the chest;
5 continue upward, head turns toward rim;
6 approach peak with tight compact hold;
7 peak tick14, both forearms still close to torso;
8 maintain the clutch hold through a slight shoulder turn;
9 begin short one-hand delivery toward imaginary hoop;
10 one-hand release at tick21, right arm snaps forward/up while left hand retracts;
11 scoring finish tick23 with right hand below rim lane;
12 descend with arms folding back;
13 land on bent knees;
14 regain ready stance.
Keep the clutch visually distinct from power dunk: hands stay close to chest through frame8, followed by a short release. Empty visible hands; no ball, hoop or rim drawn.
